tional Stock Exchange of Lithuania on the international level, to bolster confidence of domestic and foreign investors in the Lithuanian capital market.', 'The principle objectives of this Code include recommending the listed companies what basic principles they should follow in order to ensure equal understanding of transparent management and operation not only by domestic but also by foreign investors; encouraging the listed companies to improve their governance framework and disclosure of information on their activities; encouraging the listed companies to enhance quality management as a means to improve the company''s performance; promoting the activities of the listed companies on the international level and enhance confidence of domestic and foreign investors as well as other stakeholders in the companies and their governance framework and promoting activities of the National Stock Exchange of Lithuania on the international level, to bolster confidence of domestic and foreign investors in the Lithuanian capital market.', 'Lithuania', 'governance', 'in_force', '2004-01-01'::date, 'Lithuania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/104_3', ARRAY['other sustainability policy', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'lithuania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('91518435-a11a-5e79-b44e-c9501d92aaef', 'Luxembourg Chamber of Deputies Bill', 'Chamber of Deputies Bill No. 8567', 'Luxembourg''s Chamber of Deputies Bill No. 8567 aims to transpose EU directives on financial services, markets, and sustainability. It modifies existing laws to align with European regulations, focusing on transparency, environmental, social, and governance standards. Target audience includes financial institutions, corporations, and regulatory bodies.', 'Luxembourg''s Chamber of Deputies Bill No. 8567 aims to transpose EU directives on financial services, markets, and sustainability. It modifies existing laws to align with European regulations, focusing on transparency, environmental, social, and governance standards. Target audience includes financial institutions, corporations, and regulatory bodies.', 'Luxembourg''s Chamber of Deputies Bill No. 8567 aims to transpose EU directives on financial services, markets, and sustainability. It modifies existing laws to align with European regulations, focusing on transparency, environmental, social, and governance standards. Target audience includes financial institutions, corporations, and regulatory bodies.', 'Luxembourg', 'governance', 'in_force', '2025-01-01'::date, 'Luxembourg', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/105_16', ARRAY['sdg16', 'mandatory', 'luxembourg', 'regulations']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('ef17da0b-f57e-5039-a5a1-f247bbc00f3d', 'Luxembourg Bill', 'Bill No. 8591', 'Bill No. 8591 in Luxembourg aims to implement an automatic exchange of information for supplementary taxation, aligning with EU directives. It enforces a minimum effective tax rate on large multinational and national groups, requiring standardized annual information declarations for tax compliance. Targeted at entities subject to the new supplementary tax system.', 'Bill No. 8591 in Luxembourg aims to implement an automatic exchange of information for supplementary taxation, aligning with EU directives. It enforces a minimum effective tax rate on large multinational and national groups, requiring standardized annual information declarations for tax compliance. Targeted at entities subject to the new supplementary tax system.', 'Bill No. 8591 in Luxembourg aims to implement an automatic exchange of information for supplementary taxation, aligning with EU directives. It enforces a minimum effective tax rate on large multinational and national groups, requiring standardized annual information declarations for tax compliance. Targeted at entities subject to the new supplementary tax system.', 'Luxembourg', 'governance', 'in_force', '2025-01-01'::date, 'Luxembourg', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/105_18', ARRAY['mandatory', 'luxembourg', 'regulations']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('d6c63ce3-9c91-5280-bbfe-5e04085e54b3', 'Luxembourg Amendments to the Bill of Law 8370', 'Amendments to the Bill of Law 8370', 'The Amendments to the Bill of Law 8370 in Luxembourg aim to update existing laws regarding business registration, accounting, and transparency to align with EU directives on sustainability reporting. Key requirements include the establishment and publication of sustainability information by companies, with specific deadlines for compliance. The amendments apply to various sectors, particularly financial services and commercial entities, and introduce exemptions for certain organizations like the European Financial Stability Facility. The obligations outlined are mandatory for affected entities.', 'The Amendments to the Bill of Law 8370 in Luxembourg aim to update existing laws regarding business registration, accounting, and transparency to align with EU directives on sustainability reporting. Key requirements include the establishment and publication of sustainability information by companies, with specific deadlines for compliance. The amendments apply to various sectors, particularly financial services and commercial entities, and introduce exemptions for certain organizations like the European Financial Stability Facility. The obligations outlined are mandatory for affected entities.', 'The Amendments to the Bill of Law 8370 in Luxembourg aim to update existing laws regarding business registration, accounting, and transparency to align with EU directives on sustainability reporting. Key requirements include the establishment and publication of sustainability information by companies, with specific deadlines for compliance. The amendments apply to various sectors, particularly financial services and commercial entities, and introduce exemptions for certain organizations like the European Financial Stability Facility. The obligations outlined are mandatory for affected entities.', 'Luxembourg', 'climate', 'in_force', '2025-01-01'::date, 'Luxembourg', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/105_20', ARRAY['regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'luxembourg']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
